<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    What the modules' application projects do the same way, and none of them owns: today one check, of the page a
    paged query is asked for. Every module has a list that is read a page at a time, each query holds its page to
    sizes of its own, and a module does not reference another's application project; so the check all of them
    make lives here, once.

    No [assembly: Module] in this project, on purpose: it belongs to no module, so every module may name what it
    declares. It references no module and knows nothing of any of them: a query hands it its sizes and the
    refusals to answer with. Only a module's application project references it. Keep it small: a type belongs
    here only when every module's application project would otherwise carry a copy of it.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- PagingArguments: what a paged query is asked with. The package has no dependencies. -->
    <PackageReference Include="GreenDonut.Data.Primitives" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
